---
import MainLayout from "../layouts/MainLayout.astro";
import Header from "../components/Header.astro";
import Footer from "../components/Footer.astro";
import CTA from "../components/CTA.astro";
---
<MainLayout title="AC Services | Maharashtra AC Service & Repair" description="Detailed AC service, repair, installation, maintenance, gas service and specialist AC support across Pune and Mumbai.">
<Header /><main>
<section class="page-hero"><div class="container service-hero"><div><span class="eyebrow">Our Services</span><h1>Complete AC care for homes, offices & businesses.</h1><p>Explore detailed information for routine service, repairs, installation, gas-related work, maintenance and specialist AC requirements. Use the Services menu to jump directly to the support you need.</p><div class="service-hero-actions"><a class="btn btn--primary" href="/contact/">Request Service</a><a class="btn btn--secondary" href="tel:+917378351743">Call 73783 51743</a></div></div><div class="service-hero-badge"><strong>12</strong><span>AC SERVICES</span><small>PUNE • MUMBAI</small></div></div></section>
<section class="section service-directory"><div class="container"><div class="section-head"><div><span class="eyebrow">Service Directory</span><h2>Choose a service and learn what it includes.</h2><p>Each service below has practical guidance so you can describe your requirement clearly when contacting the team.</p></div></div><div class="service-list">{[
["❄","AC Service","ac-service","A planned cleaning and inspection service for everyday AC performance."],
["⚙","AC Repair","ac-repair","Troubleshooting and repair support for cooling, leakage, noise and operational problems."],
["＋","AC Installation","ac-installation","Installation support for new air conditioners with attention to placement and airflow."],
["↗","AC Uninstallation","ac-uninstallation","Careful removal when replacing, renovating or relocating an AC."],
["◌","AC Gas Filling","ac-gas-filling","Refrigerant-related inspection and service when cooling performance changes."],
["⌁","AC Gas Leakage Repair","ac-gas-leakage","Inspection and repair support when a refrigerant leak is suspected."],
["✓","AC Maintenance","ac-maintenance","Preventive care designed around cleaning, inspection and dependable operation."],
["▣","Split AC Service","split-ac-service","Dedicated service guidance for commonly used split air conditioners."],
["▤","Window AC Service","window-ac-service","Cleaning, inspection and repair support for window AC systems."],
["▥","Cassette AC Service","cassette-ac-service","Maintenance and repair support for cassette AC units in larger spaces."],
["✦","AC Not Cooling","ac-not-cooling","Diagnostic support when an AC is running but cooling is weak or uneven."],
["↻","AC Relocation","ac-relocation","Coordinated removal and installation support when an AC is moved."]
].map(([icon,title,id,short],i)=><a class="directory-card card" href={"/services/#"+id}><span class="icon">{icon}</span><strong>{String(i+1).padStart(2,"0")}</strong><h3>{title}</h3><p>{short}</p><span>Read details →</span></a>)}</div></div></section>

<section class="section section--soft detailed-services"><div class="container"><div class="section-intro"><span class="eyebrow">Detailed Service Guide</span><h2>Know what to expect from each AC service.</h2><p>Service requirements vary by AC type, condition and usage. The information below is written to help you identify the right starting point.</p></div>
<article id="ac-service" class="detail-service"><div class="detail-number">01</div><div><h2>AC Service</h2><p>AC service is a routine care process that helps keep an air conditioner clean, comfortable and ready for regular use. A typical service requirement can involve checking filters, airflow, indoor-unit cleanliness, drainage and visible operating conditions. Dust and debris can build up over time, especially when an AC is used frequently or in a dusty environment. Cleaning the accessible components can help the system move air more effectively and can make it easier to notice problems before they become disruptive.</p><p>For homes, offices and shops, planned service can be useful before periods of heavy cooling demand or whenever performance begins to feel different. If the AC has weak airflow, unusual smell, water dripping or uneven cooling, mention the symptom when making an enquiry. The right service approach depends on the AC type and its condition, so the requirement should be assessed rather than treated as a one-size-fits-all job. Customers in Pune and Mumbai can share their locality, AC type and main concern to start a clearer service request.</p></div></article>
<article id="ac-repair" class="detail-service"><div class="detail-number">02</div><div><h2>AC Repair</h2><p>AC repair is intended for situations where the air conditioner is not operating normally or a specific fault needs attention. Common signs include weak cooling, repeated shutdowns, unusual sounds, water leakage, poor airflow or an AC that does not start as expected. Repair work should begin with understanding the symptom and checking the system rather than replacing parts without a clear reason. The actual cause can vary between airflow restrictions, drainage issues, electrical components, refrigerant-related problems and other system conditions.</p><p>When requesting repair support, provide the AC type, approximate age if known, locality and the main symptom. If the unit has stopped cooling completely, explain what changed and whether it makes any unusual sound or shows any visible leakage. This information can make the enquiry more useful. In Pune and Mumbai, repair requirements can differ based on building conditions and usage, so an inspection is important before deciding the appropriate corrective work.</p></div></article>
<article id="ac-installation" class="detail-service"><div class="detail-number">03</div><div><h2>AC Installation</h2><p>AC installation is more than placing an indoor and outdoor unit on a wall. Good installation considers the room, airflow, outdoor-unit position, piping route, drainage and access for future maintenance. The goal is to create a practical setup that supports comfortable cooling while keeping the system accessible for service. Before installation, customers should consider where the indoor unit can distribute air effectively and whether the outdoor unit has adequate ventilation and a suitable mounting location.</p><p>For a new installation, share the property type, room or commercial space, preferred AC capacity if known and the Pune or Mumbai locality. If an existing unit is being replaced, mention that as well because removal and installation may need to be coordinated. Installation requirements vary between split, window and other AC types. A clear site discussion helps identify the likely work involved and reduces avoidable surprises. Proper installation also makes future cleaning, inspection and maintenance easier to plan.</p></div></article>
<article id="ac-uninstallation" class="detail-service"><div class="detail-number">04</div><div><h2>AC Uninstallation</h2><p>AC uninstallation is useful when an air conditioner needs to be removed for relocation, replacement, renovation or property work. The process should be handled carefully because an AC system includes indoor and outdoor components, connecting lines, drainage and electrical connections. A controlled removal approach helps reduce unnecessary damage to the equipment and surrounding installation area. Customers should mention whether the unit will be reinstalled at another location or is being permanently removed.</p><p>For a relocation request, provide the current locality, the destination area if known, AC type and any access details that could affect removal. The condition of the unit and existing installation can influence the work required. It is better to discuss the full requirement before disconnecting or dismantling the system yourself. In Pune and Mumbai, buildings can have different access arrangements, so information about floors, mounting positions and working space can also help. Uninstallation is often the first stage of a larger relocation or replacement job.</p></div></article>
<article id="ac-gas-filling" class="detail-service"><div class="detail-number">05</div><div><h2>AC Gas Filling</h2><p>AC gas filling is generally considered when an air conditioner shows cooling performance changes that may be connected to refrigerant level or system condition. A low refrigerant charge should not automatically be assumed to be the only reason for weak cooling. Filters, airflow, coils, drainage and other conditions can also affect performance. For that reason, refrigerant-related service should begin with checking the system and understanding why the cooling has changed.</p><p>If an AC is taking longer to cool, producing uneven cooling or repeatedly showing reduced performance, tell the service team what you have noticed and whether the problem appeared suddenly or gradually. If refrigerant is found to be low, the underlying cause should also be considered rather than treating refilling as a permanent solution. The correct refrigerant and service procedure depend on the specific AC system. Customers in Pune and Mumbai can provide the AC model information if available, along with the locality and symptoms, for a more useful enquiry.</p></div></article>
<article id="ac-gas-leakage" class="detail-service"><div class="detail-number">06</div><div><h2>AC Gas Leakage Repair</h2><p>Refrigerant leakage can affect AC cooling and may cause a system to lose performance again after a temporary refill. When leakage is suspected, the important requirement is to identify the likely leak area and address the underlying issue. Signs can include reduced cooling, repeated need for refrigerant-related service and a noticeable change in system performance. The exact cause and location require appropriate inspection because an AC can have different joints, connections and components within its refrigerant circuit.</p><p>When contacting the team, explain whether the AC was recently serviced, whether cooling dropped quickly or gradually and whether any previous gas-related work was performed. This background can help establish a useful starting point. A proper repair approach should focus on the actual condition of the system instead of repeatedly adding refrigerant without investigating why it is being lost. For homes, offices and commercial spaces in Pune and Mumbai, sharing the AC type, model information if available and locality can make the service enquiry clearer.</p></div></article>
<article id="ac-maintenance" class="detail-service"><div class="detail-number">07</div><div><h2>AC Maintenance</h2><p>AC maintenance is planned care intended to keep an air conditioner in a more predictable operating condition. Instead of waiting for a complete failure, maintenance can include cleaning, checking airflow, reviewing drainage and looking for visible signs that may affect performance. Regular attention is especially useful for ACs that run frequently in homes, offices, shops and commercial spaces. Maintenance requirements can change with usage, indoor dust, outdoor conditions and the type of AC.</p><p>A practical maintenance plan should be based on how the system is used and whether performance has changed. Customers can mention the last known service, frequency of use, AC type and any symptoms when making an enquiry. If the unit is used heavily during summer, planning service before peak demand can be more convenient than waiting for a problem. Maintenance does not guarantee that every fault will be prevented, but it can provide an opportunity to notice common issues earlier. Pune and Mumbai customers can use the dedicated city pages for local coverage information.</p></div></article>
<article id="split-ac-service" class="detail-service"><div class="detail-number">08</div><div><h2>Split AC Service</h2><p>Split AC service focuses on the indoor and outdoor units that make up a split air-conditioning system. Routine care can include cleaning accessible areas, checking airflow, inspecting drainage and considering the general condition of the system. Because the indoor and outdoor units work together, a change in cooling performance should not be judged only from the indoor unit. Dust, blocked airflow, drainage concerns and other conditions can influence everyday operation.</p><p>For a split AC enquiry, share the number of units, approximate usage, locality and the main concern. If there are multiple ACs in a home or office, it can also help to mention whether the issue affects one unit or several. Service needs can vary between a lightly used home AC and a heavily used commercial system. A clear description helps the service requirement start with the right context. Customers across Pune and Mumbai can use the city service pages to identify their coverage area before contacting the team.</p></div></article>
<article id="window-ac-service" class="detail-service"><div class="detail-number">09</div><div><h2>Window AC Service</h2><p>Window AC service is focused on the requirements of a single-unit air conditioner installed through or near a window opening. Dust accumulation, restricted airflow, drainage concerns and general wear can affect the unit over time. Routine cleaning and inspection can help maintain everyday performance and can make it easier to notice changes such as weak cooling, unusual noise or water-related problems. Because the unit is installed in a fixed opening, access and surrounding space can also matter when service is planned.</p><p>When enquiring about window AC service, provide the AC capacity or model if known, the locality and the main issue. If the unit is difficult to access, mention the installation position so the service requirement can be understood more clearly. Window ACs can have different maintenance needs depending on usage and environment. Customers in Pune and Mumbai can request service for homes, offices, shops and other suitable spaces. If the unit is no longer economical to maintain and replacement is being considered, uninstallation can also be discussed as part of the requirement.</p></div></article>
<article id="cassette-ac-service" class="detail-service"><div class="detail-number">10</div><div><h2>Cassette AC Service</h2><p>Cassette AC service is designed for ceiling-mounted cassette systems commonly used in offices, shops, commercial spaces and larger rooms. These systems distribute air across a wider area, so airflow and cleanliness can have a noticeable effect on comfort. Service requirements can include cleaning accessible components, checking airflow, reviewing drainage and considering the condition of the indoor and outdoor system. The exact work depends on the model, installation arrangement and current condition.</p><p>Commercial ACs can also operate for longer hours than residential units, making planned maintenance useful. When requesting cassette AC service, mention the number of units, location, operating hours if relevant and any symptoms such as weak airflow, uneven cooling, water leakage or unusual noise. Access to ceiling units should also be considered when planning the visit. Customers across Pune and Mumbai can provide the building type and locality so the enquiry starts with appropriate context. Regular service can help identify maintenance needs before they become a larger interruption to a workplace or commercial space.</p></div></article>
<article id="ac-not-cooling" class="detail-service"><div class="detail-number">11</div><div><h2>AC Not Cooling</h2><p>An AC that is running but not cooling properly can have several possible causes, so the symptom should be investigated rather than immediately assuming a gas problem. Airflow restrictions, dirty filters, drainage concerns, refrigerant-related conditions, outdoor-unit issues and other system faults can all influence cooling. The first useful step is to describe what changed: whether the AC stopped cooling suddenly, gradually became weaker or only cools one part of the room.</p><p>Customers can check basic settings and unobstructed airflow, but recurring or significant cooling problems are better discussed with a service professional. When making an enquiry, share the AC type, locality, approximate age if known and whether there are other symptoms such as water leakage, noise or repeated shutdowns. This information helps narrow the starting point. For Pune and Mumbai customers, the dedicated service-area pages can help identify local coverage. Prompt attention can also reduce the chance of continuing to operate an AC while an unresolved issue is affecting its performance.</p></div></article>
<article id="ac-relocation" class="detail-service"><div class="detail-number">12</div><div><h2>AC Relocation</h2><p>AC relocation is useful when an air conditioner needs to move from one room, property or installation position to another. The process normally involves careful uninstallation followed by planning the new installation. The new location may require a different piping route, drainage arrangement, mounting position and access plan. Because these details affect the final setup, relocation should be treated as a complete service requirement rather than simply moving the indoor unit.</p><p>When enquiring, share the current location, destination locality, AC type, number of units and whether the destination is in the same building or a different property. Mention any known access limitations as well. If the AC is being relocated during renovation or a move, timing can be coordinated around the broader work. Customers in Pune and Mumbai can use the relevant city pages to identify local coverage. A clear relocation enquiry helps determine the likely removal, transport and reinstallation requirements before the work begins.</p></div></article>
</div></section>

<section class="section"><div class="container service-bottom-grid"><div><span class="eyebrow">Before You Book</span><h2>Make your enquiry more useful.</h2><p>Tell us your Pune or Mumbai locality, AC type, number of units and the main problem. If known, include the model, approximate age and last service date.</p></div><div class="service-checks"><span>✓ City & locality</span><span>✓ AC type</span><span>✓ Main symptom</span><span>✓ Number of units</span><span>✓ Installation or repair requirement</span><span>✓ Preferred contact method</span></div></div></section>
</main><CTA /><Footer /></MainLayout>
